---
/* L01 - three question types, three answer shapes, one measurement path.
   One writer: the figures workstream E. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L01.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a clinic reception counter with three trays on it: one tray holding a single blank slip, one holding four blank folders, and one holding a small four-rung ladder with a round marker on the second rung."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L01-fig-title L01-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L01-fig-title">Three question types, three answer shapes, one pair out</title>
      <desc id="L01-fig-desc">
        Three panels side by side. The first, labelled noul, holds a horizontal scale from zero to one
        with a marker at 0.9 and a dashed threshold at 0.5. The second, labelled choice, holds four
        option boxes - billing, technical, other and sales - with billing filled in and the rest
        outlined, showing four unordered options and one chosen label. The third, labelled score,
        holds a ladder of four ordered rungs numbered 3, 2, 1 and 0, from Critical down to No impact,
        with a marker on rung 1. Three lines run down from the panels and meet at one box reading
        one pair, probability and outcome, which is what Brier and ECE are computed from.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L01-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- panel 1: noul -->
      <rect x="24" y="48" width="190" height="184" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="36" y="72" class="fig-head">noul</text>
      <line x1="44" y1="120" x2="184" y2="120" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="40" y="140" class="fig-num">0</text>
      <text x="180" y="140" class="fig-num">1</text>
      <line x1="114" y1="100" x2="114" y2="140" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      <text x="114" y="94" class="fig-num fig-num--prussian" text-anchor="middle">0.5</text>
      <circle cx="170" cy="120" r="4.5" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text x="170" y="110" class="fig-num" text-anchor="middle">0.9</text>
      <text x="36" y="176" class="fig-text">one number</text>
      <text x="36" y="190" class="fig-text">0.9 means 90% yes</text>
      <text x="36" y="204" class="fig-text">the threshold 0.5</text>
      <text x="36" y="218" class="fig-text">is a policy</text>

      <!-- panel 2: choice -->
      <rect x="224" y="48" width="190" height="184" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="236" y="72" class="fig-head">choice</text>
      <rect x="236" y="88" width="80" height="28" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="246" y="106" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">billing</text>
      <rect x="326" y="88" width="80" height="28" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="336" y="106" class="fig-text">technical</text>
      <rect x="236" y="124" width="80" height="28" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="246" y="142" class="fig-text">sales</text>
      <rect x="326" y="124" width="80" height="28" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="336" y="142" class="fig-text">other</text>
      <text x="236" y="176" class="fig-text">one label of four</text>
      <text x="236" y="190" class="fig-text">unordered, so wrong is</text>
      <text x="236" y="204" class="fig-text">wrong, and a probability</text>
      <text x="236" y="218" class="fig-text">for every option</text>

      <!-- panel 3: score -->
      <rect x="424" y="48" width="190" height="184" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule-soft)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="436" y="72" class="fig-head">score</text>
      <line x1="452" y1="88" x2="452" y2="168" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="452" y1="92" x2="520" y2="92" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="452" y1="116" x2="520" y2="116" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="452" y1="140" x2="520" y2="140" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="452" y1="164" x2="520" y2="164" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="444" y="96" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">3</text>
      <text x="444" y="120" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">2</text>
      <text x="444" y="144" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">1</text>
      <text x="444" y="168" class="fig-num" text-anchor="end">0</text>
      <text x="528" y="96" class="fig-text">Critical</text>
      <text x="528" y="120" class="fig-text">Major</text>
      <text x="528" y="144" class="fig-text">Minor</text>
      <text x="528" y="168" class="fig-text">No impact</text>
      <circle cx="486" cy="140" r="4.5" fill="var(--color-prussian)" />
      <text x="436" y="192" class="fig-text">one index into an</text>
      <text x="436" y="206" class="fig-text">ordered list of four</text>
      <text x="436" y="220" class="fig-text">the gold is index 1</text>

      <!-- the one measurement path -->
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 200; --m-duration: 1.1s;" d="M 119 236 C 119 256, 200 248, 246 268" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L01-arrow)" />
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 40; --m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.25s;" d="M 319 236 L 319 268" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L01-arrow)" />
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 200; --m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" d="M 519 236 C 519 256, 438 248, 392 268" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L01-arrow)" />
      <rect x="180" y="272" width="280" height="52" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="196" y="294" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">one pair: probability, outcome</text>
      <text x="196" y="312" class="fig-text">what Brier and ECE are computed from</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L01</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">A noul, a choice and a score look nothing alike on the wire, but each one ends as the same pair - a probability and an outcome - and that pair is what the metrics read.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-num--prussian {
    fill: var(--color-prussian);
  }
</style>
